  "explanation": {
    "en": "〜枚 (まい) is the counter for flat, thin objects like paper, shirts, tickets, or plates. The pronunciation does not change with the number.\n\nKey points:\n• Use 〜枚 for flat items\n• Same reading for all numbers: いちまい, にまい, さんまい\n• Common for paper, shirts, tickets\n• Easy and regular\n\nExample: “切符を二枚買いました” means “I bought two tickets.”\n\nBecause the reading is regular, 〜枚 is one of the easiest counters to use.\n\nPractice by counting paper and shirts: 紙を三枚, シャツを二枚.",
    "ja": ""
  },
